5. Write a code example where enum iteration triggers specific logic (method calls) for each constant.
-->Program:
public class Main {

    // Nested enum
    enum TrafficSignal {
        RED,
        YELLOW,
        GREEN;

        // Custom method with specific logic
        public void action() {
            switch (this) {
                case RED:
                    System.out.println("Stop");
                    break;

                case YELLOW:
                    System.out.println("Get Ready");
                    break;

                case GREEN:
                    System.out.println("Go");
                    break;
            }
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Iterate through enum constants
        for (TrafficSignal signal : TrafficSignal.values()) {

            System.out.print(signal + " : ");
            signal.action();   // Calls different logic for each constant
        }
    }
}
Output:
RED : Stop
YELLOW : Get Ready
GREEN : Go
Explanation:
TrafficSignal is an enum with three constants.
The action() method contains different logic for each constant using a switch.
TrafficSignal.values() returns all enum constants.
During iteration, signal.action() executes the corresponding logic for each constant.
Flow:
TrafficSignal.values()

Returns:

{RED, YELLOW, GREEN}

Loop execution:

RED.action();      // Stop
YELLOW.action();   // Get Ready
GREEN.action();    // Go
Key Points:
✅ An enum can contain custom methods.
✅ Each enum constant can trigger different logic.
✅ values() is used to iterate over all enum constants.
